  "verdict": "ESP/HF are matched-input, shifted-label cells: the sgRNA sets are ~98% shared with WT, so the covariate-shift density ratio is 1 by construction and weighted conformal reduces to split conformal. The published 'weighting cannot repair the shift' conclusion is therefore untestable on those cells, not false; the genuinely shifted cells are HELA/HCT116/HL60 (3-4% overlap). On every cell the effective remedy is recalibration on a small number of target-domain labels, which is reported here as a cohort-size curve."
